    <!-- Legal -->
    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy policy</string>
    <string name="terms_title">Terms &amp; disclaimer</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">Last updated: 2 October 2026\n\nWinterArc is designed to work entirely on your device.\n\nWhat we store\nYour goals, check-ins, notes, milestones and preferences are stored locally on this device.\n\nYour account\nTo create an account you provide your mobile number. It is sent to our authentication provider (Google Firebase Authentication) only to deliver a one-time code by SMS and to sign you in. We do not use your number for marketing, and it is never shown to other people.\n\nWhat we share\nYour goals, notes and history stay on this device; this version does not upload them. Your mobile number is shared with Firebase Authentication for verification only. Analytics and crash reporting are disabled.\n\nBackups\nIf you use Android\'s device backup, your WinterArc data may be included in that backup under your Google account, according to your device settings.\n\nNotifications\nReminders are scheduled on your device. No reminder content leaves your device.\n\nDeleting your data\nYou can delete any goal from the archive. Uninstalling the app removes all data stored on this device. To delete your account and the phone number held by the authentication provider, contact the developer through the app\'s store listing.\n\nChanges\nIf a future version adds optional cloud sync or analytics, this policy will be updated and you will be asked before any data is shared.\n\nContact\nQuestions about privacy can be sent to the developer through the app\'s store listing.</string>
    <string name="terms_body">Last updated: 2 October 2026\n\nNot medical advice\nWinterArc is a personal goal tracker. It does not provide medical, health, fitness or coaching advice, and it cannot assess whether an activity is safe for you.\n\nYour responsibility\nChoose targets that suit your current ability and health. Increase gradually, include rest days, and stop if you feel pain, dizziness or discomfort. If you have a health condition, are pregnant, or are returning after injury, consider speaking with a qualified health professional before starting a new activity plan.\n\nSafety notices\nThe app may show gentle notices for plans that increase quickly or involve long distances. These notices are general information, not a diagnosis or a personalised assessment.\n\nContent\nFacts and quotations in the app include their source. General encouraging messages are written by WinterArc and are not attributed to any person.\n\nNo warranty\nThe app is provided as is. While we work hard to keep your data safe, please keep device backups if your history is important to you.\n\nChanges\nThese terms may be updated in future versions of the app.</string>

